== what the numbers say
1. The whole app costs 3.22732 DERO to install at these sizes: 35 DOCs at ring 2 and one ring-16 INDEX. The INDEX is
   2.2% of it; the DOCs are the cost, and each one is its gzip size plus 339 to 375 gas.
2. Two DOCs are close to the per-transaction storage-gas limit of 20,000 (deploy/README.md §4): feed.js at 19,712
   (288 left) and wrap.js at 19,660 (340 left). genconfig's own DOC size check agrees: feed.js is 18,128 B against its
   18,432 B limit. A few hundred more gzipped bytes in either file and that file needs splitting before the bundle can
   be installed at all.
3. xswd.js could not be estimated. The daemon's gas estimate hit the graviton ':' bucket panic five times, and
   telainstall sent the DOC with its size-based fallback fee of 6,224. It was mined at height 276 and paid 6,224. By
   the other 34 DOCs' ratio its gas would be about 5,545, so the fallback overpaid about 680 atomic units (0.0068 DERO)
   and changed nothing else.
